  "body": "**The request (mkinney, 2026-11-15):** \"What about example images for various things?\"\n\nThe whole site has 2 images. Pages such as Setups, Workholding, the operation pages and Multi-axis would be much clearer with pictures.\n\nWanted:\n- Example images rendered from CamCraft itself: the viewport with stock, part, fixture and toolpath; the operation page with its key parameters; before/after views where a setting changes the path (a stepover, a ramp entry or helix, a lead-in).\n- Make them reproducibly: an off-screen render with the UI test harness (`egui_kittest`, as the PR screenshot renders do) from a committed demo project, through one script (`cargo xtask docs-images` or similar). Images go in `site/static/images/guide/` and are regenerated at each docs review (#1792 style), not by hand.\n- Clean room: only CamCraft renders and original diagrams. Never images or text from HSMWorks, Fusion or vendor manuals.\n- Keep the files small (PNG, about 1200 px wide, optimised). Every image has alt text.\n\nNot the same as PR review screenshots: those stay on the `pr-screenshots` branch (#1794, #1845). Guide images belong in `site/static/`.\n\nDone means: at least the Setups, Workholding, 2D, 3D and Multi-axis pages have rendered examples from one script, and the script runs without a display (CI, xvfb).\n",
